@@ -62,6 +63,13 @@ The assertions are `toBe`, `toEqual` (deep), `toBeNear`, `toBeTruthy` and `toThr
 - **Every selected spec runs.** An affected gate runs the specs the watch map lists, a full gate every fast-tier spec, a slow gate only `z-nile/tests/slow.tsv`. Nothing is skipped because an earlier run passed. The same commit and the same change do the same work on any machine. The runner packs files by `<home>/.cache/spec-durations.tsv` (one line `<seconds>\t<path>`), a hint written after a run and safe to delete: with no file the run is ordered by path. `slow.tsv` is the committed list of specs those two gates skip, in the same line grammar; its seconds are not the live times.
 - **Watch miss**: a spec fails under `--full` but wasn't selected for the same diff. That's a hole in the map, a chore (z-ticket). `./zn watch-net` fills it and captures it, though it still types the capture a defect (d0353).
 
+## Suites
+Two suites share the repository (c0083). The **harness suite** is the tooling's specs: z-nile's home (`z-nile/tests/`, its promoted `acceptance/` specs and every spec that watches tooling or root files). The **game suite** is every game project's: `pickman`, `arcade`, `portal`, `snake`, `invaders` and `asteroids`. A spec's suite is where it lives, its home, and a promoted acceptance spec goes to its item's project's home whatever the item's type (`./zn done`). No spec moves between suites and no tag is needed. `z-nile/lib/suites.luau` is the one reader: `suites.of(project)` (a project no game list names is harness, so new tooling is never skipped), `suites.projects`, `suites.changed` and `suites.crossings`.
+- **A change runs a suite only when it touches that suite's files.** `--affected` runs the specs the watch map lists, and a watch file keeps its spec to its own suite's paths (`watch.forSuite`: a game spec's list holds paths under a game home, a tooling spec's every other path: z-nile, the root's files, `zn`, `scripts/`, `.github/`), which `lune run z-nile/watch-check` enforces in every gate that runs specs: a watch file naming the other suite's path fails, naming the spec and the path. So a game change selects no tooling spec and a tooling change no game spec. A mixed change is the union of its paths.
+- **A path's suite is its location** (`suites.changed`): under a game home it is the game's, under z-nile or under no home (a root file, `zn`, the root's `scripts/` and configs, a document at the top) the harness's, and a tracker document (under a project root) none, because it selects no spec. The root configs (`.luaurc`, `selene.toml`, `stylua.toml`, `rokit.toml`) and `zn` still force every project's static stages, which `--suite changed` does not narrow.
+- **`--suite`** limits a gate to one suite's projects: `harness` or `game` narrow the static stages and the specs, in every mode but `--slow`. `all` is no flag at all. `changed` (the suites the change touches, from `lune run z-nile/affected -- --suite changed [--base REF]`) narrows the specs of a `--full` run to those suites' projects, and leaves `--affected` and `--static` as the bare gate, which already selects by the watch map. `--full --suite changed` is every fast-tier spec of each suite the change touches, which a bare `--full` (every project) is not.
+- **When both suites run**: `setup.sh`, the merge of a pull request that changes a game (the clean clone's bare `--full`, which runs every project: the user's decision that the merge's full gate runs all for real so that a watch-map gap in either direction shows, c0239), and the net after each landing (`./zn watch-net`, every project's fast suite on main). Every other gate step is affected-only, and a tooling pull request's merge runs `--affected` on the branch.
+
